# EZD-205 · Rooms and closure (split proposal)

- **ACs:** AC-EZD-205-1 … AC-EZD-205-6 (`vault/spec/acceptance-criteria.md:706-711`, stage-0), shared out to the parts below
- **Complexity:** high (each part; reasons per part)
- **Areas:** geometry, data-model, testing
- **User-visible result:** none on screen from either part; EZD-210 (Wall and Room rectangle tools) and EZD-207 (Plan canvas) show rooms, areas and the gap box built on these functions.
- Phase: 4 · Planned by: planner · Date: 2026-11-05 · Status: split proposal

## Split proposal

**Why.** Planned whole, the ticket touches about 33 files and needs about 30 tests, over the size rule (PROCESS.md section 6 "Ticket size": about 20 files, about 25 tests; Josh 2026-10-22). Sources of the count:
- ticket row (`vault/tickets/phases/phase-02.md:11`) and AC-EZD-205-1 to -6;
- the room schema change is a `schema_version` bump: P202 Version rule and 03b rule 5 need a migrate step, a new stored sample and edits to the earlier tests that pin the version (P203 step 5, T22, T23, E1);
- Q-0576 (answered-agent): EZD-205 adds the S03 room label (`NAME · N SF`) to EZD-238's drawing list. Board `vault/mockups/S03Plan.png` (HTML `html/project/S03Plan.dc.html`) draws it in Instrument Sans 600, 15 px, letter-spacing 1.5 px. P238's text item knows only `font: 'dm-mono-400'` and its metrics generator reads one font file (P238 section 3; P238 steps 3–4), so the label needs a second metrics table and the generator change;
- Q-0568 and ARCH Events: `room.closure_overridden` is emitted through the registry now, and "a new name goes into `EVENTS` in the same commit as its first emitter". `emit` is server-only (`app/src/server/events/`), so the emitter is EZD-120a's save route (`POST /api/projects/[id]/objects`, P120a section 3). The route needs the stored room to tell a new override from an unchanged one;
- Q-0568: "plans decide … room storage with area derived". The stored rooms must follow the walls (a reconcile step every wall-changing tool calls: EZD-210, EZD-212, EZD-311);
- `app/src/lib/events/registry.test.ts` T1 (`INTERNAL` `toHaveLength(34)`) and T3 (`toEqual` on the internal set) pin the registry (read 2026-11-05).

The work splits into two lettered parts, built a → b. Each part is planned as its own unit from its section here.

### Part EZD-205a · Room outlines, area, storage and label
- **Scope (schema):** the room schema gains `status` (Existing while walls are, Q-0558) and `closureOverride` (who, when, gap; `null` when none) (Q-0570, decisions 03; 03b rule 5). `CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION` 2 → 3 with a v2 → v3 migrate step: rooms get `status: 'existing'` and `closureOverride: null`, other objects unchanged. A stored sample `schema/samples/v3.json` is added (P202 Version rule, `migrationChainProblems`; P203 step 5 pattern). Wall data is unchanged.
- **Scope (outlines):** pure functions in `packages/geometry/src/rooms/`. They find every closed space the walls of one level enclose, crossings and T joins included: "a wall dividing a room makes two rooms; a wall crossing a wall joins at the crossing" (Q-0570; Q-0598: a crossing is a join, which EZD-203 `findWallJoins` already reports as `{ kind: 'cross', otherId }` with no `end` or `otherEnd` (P203 Decided Joins; section 3 `WallJoin`); EZD-205 consumes these joins and creates none). Each outline runs along the inside finished face of every bounding wall, from P203 `wallFaceLines`. Thickness goes outside the room (Q-0559); a partition is centred on its line, so its faces sit 2 1/4" each side (Q-0569 (b); 09j Thickness side row 4). Axes are +x east, +y north (P203 Decided Axes). Points compare with `pointsEqual` / `coordsEqual`, 1/64" inclusive (P202 `tolerance.ts`; 03g).
- **Scope (area):** area comes from the outline (shoelace, square inches ÷ 144), in whole square feet with halves going up (Q-0207; Q-0568; 03g halfway rule). It is never stored (Q-0568 "area derived"; 11 rule 2).
- **Scope (storage):** one reconcile function. Given the model objects of a level, it returns the room creates, updates and deletes that make the stored rooms match the outlines. It keeps a room's id, name and override when its outline moves (stable ids, P202). A new room is named `Room N` (Q-0568). Every wall-changing tool calls it (EZD-210, EZD-212, EZD-311 rows). Part a's plan states the rule that matches stored rooms to outlines. It also says which room keeps the id and name when a partition splits one room into two (AC-EZD-205-5); if no source decides it, it asks a QP question.
- **Scope (label):** EZD-238's drawing list adds one text item per room, in layer `rooms`. Its text is `NAME · N SF`, in capitals as on board S03 (Q-0568, Q-0570, Q-0576 (a)). The style comes from the board: Instrument Sans 600, 15 px, letter-spacing 1.5 px. The font file `app/src/styles/fonts/instrument-sans-latin-600-normal.woff2` is committed (read 2026-11-05). P238's metrics generator and `DrawingItem` `font` union gain this font. Part a's plan decides how letter-spacing enters `widthPt`, the label's anchor point, and the view field for its size (the board's 15 px against P238 `dimensionTextPt`).
- **Done when:** AC-EZD-205-1 and AC-EZD-205-5, verbatim. Then: a room object holds its status and its closure override, and a stored room of schema version 2 loads through migrate with status Existing and no override (Q-0570; 03b rule 5). The drawing list gives each room the label `NAME · N SF` in capitals (Q-0576; Q-0568; Q-0570; board S03).
- **Depends on:** EZD-203 (row). Missing from the ticket row: EZD-202 (room schema, `tolerance.ts`, migrate; through EZD-203); EZD-238 (drawing list and metrics generator, Q-0576; phase 3, merged before phase 4).
- **Files (about 18):**
  - `packages/geometry/src/schema/room.ts`, `schema/migrate.ts`, `schema/samples/v3.json`;
  - `src/rooms/outlines.ts`, `area.ts`, `sync.ts`, `index.ts`; `src/index.ts`;
  - `src/drawing/build.ts`, `drawing/text.ts`, `scripts/font-metrics.mjs`, `drawing/font-metrics.generated.ts`;
  - a rooms test fixture file; four new test files;
  - earlier-test edits (test-author, before the builder; L-021, L-049), each against the file as EZD-203 leaves it:
    - P202 `migrate.test.ts` `STORED_SAMPLES` (add 3: `./samples/v3.json`; P203 E1 adds 2);
    - P203 T22/T23 (version 2 → 3, v3.json);
    - P203 E2: `packages/geometry/src/schema/schema.test.ts` G5 refuses version 3 after EZD-203; version 3 is now valid, so the refused version input becomes 4 (expected `unknown_schema_version` unchanged);
    - P203 E3: `app/src/server/model/model-schema.test.ts` A3 sends `schemaVersion` 3 after EZD-203; it becomes 4 (title text "schemaVersion 3" → "schemaVersion 4", expected `unknown_schema_version` unchanged). A1 (and any other test in the file that sends a room, as at line 339 today; `roomData` reads `copyOf('room', …)`, line 122): any room sent at `CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION` gains `status: 'existing'` and `closureOverride: null` by the v2 → v3 rule above; expected `schema_version` already reads `CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION` (P203 E3);
    - P238 T4 (generated file and key count);
    - part a's plan reruns P203 E5's grep with `schemaVersion: 3` and `schema_version: 2` added, and names each further hit with its new value;
  - `docs/architecture.md` `### Drawing list (EZD-238)` (rooms, label font).
  - The plan also greps non-test code that builds room `data` (P203 step 11 pattern) and updates every hit. EZD-236's benchmark generator is the likely one if it merges first.
- **Tests (about 15):** the 10 rows of 09j Room area (165, 123, 108, 60, 48 and 68 SF included); the half-up boundary (122.5 → 123) and 0.25 → 0; outline finding for a rectangle, an L, a triangle, a partition split, a crossing wall and an open chain (no room); face offsets for `right`, `left` and `center` walls; a level filter; the reconcile cases (create `Room N`, keep id and name on a moved outline, split, delete); migrate v2 → v3 and v3.json; schema refusals (bad status, malformed override); the label text and font item.
- **Complexity:** high. Planar-face finding is a new algorithm every room, area and takeoff ticket builds on, and the ticket carries a schema migration and the shared font-metrics generator (PROCESS.md section 4). Test-author Sonnet 5.5, builder Opus 5.5.
- **security-review: no.** Pure geometry and a schema shape; no route, table, permission or money.
- **Reviewers:** code-reviewer · calc-auditor yes (areas, outlines) · ui-verifier no · security-reviewer no.
- **Visual checklist:** none. The drawing list is data; EZD-207's canvas draws it.
- **Proposed wording:** none expected. `Room N` and `NAME · N SF` are decided (Q-0568; board S03).

### Part EZD-205b · Closure gap, absorb and keep out of square
- **Scope (closure):** pure functions over a level's walls. They find each open wall chain (walls joined end to end by corners, P203 `findWallJoins`) and report:
  - **closed:** three or more walls whose end misses its start by 1/64" or less (`pointsEqual`; 03g; Q-0568);
  - **gap:** a miss over 1/64" and at most 12" in a straight line, inclusive (Q-0562; Q-0568; Q-0569 (c)). The report gives the gap vector, the straight-line size, and the display size to the nearest 1/16" with halves up, never 0": a gap that rounds to 0" reads 1/16" (Q-0570; 09j Closure rows 2–4, 6, 8);
  - **open:** a miss farther than 12", or fewer than three walls; no room (Q-0570; 09j Closure rows 5, 7, 9).
  The gap is worked out from the walls, so it comes back after reload (Q-0570, decisions 05).
- **Scope (absorb):** only a wall of that chain that runs parallel to the gap can absorb it (Q-0568; S02 Decisions: any wall of the room, adjacent or not). Its length changes by the gap, and the walls after it in the chain move by the gap vector, so corners stay joined (09j Absorbing rows 1, 2). Absorb is refused for:
  - a wall across the gap (row 3);
  - a wall of another room or of no chain (row 4; Q-0570);
  - a change that leaves any wall at 0" or over 200' (row 5; Q-0570; P203 `wallLengthProblem`).
  When no wall of the chain is parallel, only Keep out of square is offered (Q-0569 (c); 09j Closure row 6). Part b's plan states "parallel" with the 1/64" rule across the wall. It also says how "a miss in both directions" (Q-0569 (c)) reads for a room with angled walls, or asks a QP question. Absorb returns the changed walls, and the part-a reconcile step then makes the room.
- **Scope (keep out of square):** the room is stored with its outline closed across the gap (area as part a; 09j Keep out of square: 120 SF). Its `closureOverride` holds who, when and the gap vector (Q-0568; Q-0570). The override clears, and the gap shows again, when a later edit changes the gap: the part-a reconcile step compares the stored gap with the recomputed one by `pointsEqual` (Q-0568; AC-EZD-205-4).
- **Scope (event):** `room.closure_overridden` joins `EVENTS` as `internal` (Q-0570, decisions 07), with payload `{ roomId, gapIn, userId }` (S02 Events: room id, gap size, user) narrowed in `EventPayloads` (ARCH Events). The test-author edits `registry.test.ts`: T1 `INTERNAL` gains the name and its length goes 34 → 35; T3 stays `toEqual` on the new set (lesson L-049).
  The save route emits the event once for each saved room whose override is new or changed against the stored row. The stored row is read under the user's RLS before the save; its `updated_seq` equals the change's `baseSeq`, or the save conflicts (P120a M5 step 8). `userId` is the session's app user.
  A room change whose new override names another user as "who" is refused: 400 `invalid_object` with a new `ObjectIssueCode` (P202 section 3), so the stored "who" cannot drift from the user who saved it (CLAUDE.md rule 18). Emit failure is handled as `model.saved` is (P120a Decided Event: `reportError`, still 200).
- **Done when:** AC-EZD-205-2, AC-EZD-205-3, AC-EZD-205-4 and AC-EZD-205-6, verbatim. The ticket row's "Room closure acceptance test passes as a unit test" is AC-2 to AC-4 with 12 Room closure.
- **Depends on:** EZD-205a. Missing from the ticket row: EZD-120a (save route, `model_object`, M5 conflict rule; through EZD-202); EZD-022 (registry, merged); EZD-102 (route guards, merged); EZD-024 (`reportError`, merged).
- **Files (about 14):**
  - `packages/geometry/src/rooms/closure.ts`, `absorb.ts`, `override.ts`, `sync.ts` (override clear), `index.ts`;
  - `packages/geometry/src/schema/index.ts` (issue code);
  - `app/src/lib/events/registry.ts`;
  - `app/src/server/model/model.ts` (override check and event list);
  - `app/src/app/api/projects/[id]/objects/route.ts`;
  - test files `rooms/closure.test.ts`, `absorb.test.ts`, `override.test.ts`; the save-route test (P120a R1 file, new describe); the `registry.test.ts` edit;
  - `docs/architecture.md` `### Events` (one line: who emits `room.closure_overridden`).
- **Tests (about 16):** the nine rows of 09j Closure; the five rows of 09j Absorbing (row 2: 119.5 SF shown as 120 SF); the 1/64" and 12" boundaries on grid values (03g "Tests at the exact boundary use grid values only"); keep out of square storing who, when and gap with area 120 SF; override cleared by a gap-changing edit and kept by an edit that does not change the gap; registry T1/T3 edit; save route: one emit for a new override, none for an unchanged one, 400 for another user's "who", emit throw still 200.
- **Complexity:** high. New geometry with refusals, plus a change to the shared save route that reads stored rows and refuses data: data integrity and API (PROCESS.md section 4). Test-author Sonnet 5.5, builder Opus 5.5.
- **security-review: yes** (API, data access: the save route's prior read under RLS and the refusal of another user's "who").
- **Reviewers:** code-reviewer · calc-auditor yes (gap sizes, absorb lengths) · ui-verifier no · security-reviewer yes.
- **Visual checklist:** none. EZD-210 builds the gap box (Q-0569, decisions 05).
- **Proposed wording:** none expected. Refusals are reason codes; EZD-210's plan words the messages (09j Absorbing row 3 "Refused with a message"), and the 400 reuses `error.invalid_input` (P202 section 3).

### Applies to both parts
- Code lives in `packages/geometry/src/rooms/`, re-exported from `@ezdraft/geometry` (ARCH Folder layout: `packages/geometry/` pure TypeScript, no UI). Only part b touches `app/`.
- Numbers are taken from 09j and the decisions, never from mockup sample data (KNOWN-LIMITS 5).
- Lessons each plan applies:
  - earlier tests that pin the schema version, the samples, the font table or the registry are named as test-author edits with new values (EZD-021; L-049; L-021 inventory);
  - fixtures satisfy the changed room type (L-042);
  - list checks use `toContain` where a later ticket adds entries (L-024);
  - every test row names the wrong implementation it rejects (L-050);
  - empty, extreme and malformed inputs get their own rows (L-052);
  - helpers named with their file path (L-043);
  - test count and titles fixed (L-034);
  - no test reads a document (L-041).

### Ledger notes for the orchestrator
- Dependents that list base `EZD-205` expand to both parts (KNOWN-LIMITS 9): EZD-210 (`phase-02.md:16`), EZD-235 (`phase-02.md:41`; needs only 205a's areas), EZD-311 (`phase-03.md:19`).
- Slice 4 build order (PHASES.md Slice 4) becomes 201, 203, 205a, 205b, 206, 236, 207, 209, 210, 221. The Phase 4 Build gate's "ACs of EZD-201, 203, 205" covers both parts (`phase-02.md:3`).
- EZD-236 (benchmark generator) builds room objects and depends only on EZD-202. 205a's plan updates any room literal it finds (scope above), so no ledger change is needed.

## Sources
- Ticket: `phase-02.md:11`; `tickets.json` EZD-205; PHASES.md Slice 4 (Josh's test script steps 2, 3, 7).
- Spec: 09e Geometry and drafting rules; 09j (Typed lengths limits, Thickness side, Room area, Closure, Absorbing a gap, Keep out of square); 03f; 03g; S02 Controls, Validation, Events, Decisions; 12 Room closure; 07 Internal app events; 00e glossary (Closure gap, Absorb, Out of square: code names fall to these plans).
- Decisions: Q-0207, Q-0558, Q-0559, Q-0562, Q-0568, Q-0569, Q-0570 (`decisions/09-calculations-and-rules.md`); Q-0568, Q-0569, Q-0570 (`decisions/05-screens.md`); Q-0570 (`decisions/03-data-model.md`, `decisions/07-hooks-events-and-integrations.md`); Q-0576 (`QUESTIONS-answered.md:359`). Rounds 24–26 (13a, 13b): no row on rooms or closure. Open Q-0583 (EZD-203 T joins) does not change either part.
- Dependency contracts (section 3 of each): P202, P203 (plus its Decided Axes, Face offsets, Joins, Move rows and steps 1, 5, 11), P238 (plus its font rows), P120a (plus Decided Event, M5), P022.
- Code read 2026-11-05: `app/src/lib/events/registry.ts`, `registry.test.ts` (T1, T3), `packages/geometry/src/index.ts`, `app/src/styles/fonts/`, board S03 HTML (room label style).
- Research: no report covers this ticket (no retriever dispatched).
- Architecture: none beyond the core for this proposal; read Events. Part a's plan adds `Drawing list (EZD-238)`; part b's adds `Events`.

## Open questions
None at the split level; each part plan raises its own (part a: which room keeps the name on a split, if no source decides; part b: "both directions" for angled walls, if no source decides).
